    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (the sole `AcceptanceTest`) passes and the project builds successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `bulkSignupWarning` on the `POST /api/owners` create pipeline, surfaced on the owner response/`GET`.\n\n**How it works:** a new pipeline step counts owners already registered on the request's adjusted business day (the same `registrationDate` accumulation path used by the daily-limit rule) and, running before the owner is saved (so it never counts itself), sets a persisted boolean: `true` when that count is **> 80**, else `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `bulkSignupWarning` column field with getter/setter (mirrors `namesakeCount`).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n- `function/owner/AssignBulkSignupWarning.java` \u2014 new OfficeFloor function computing the flag (threshold 80, excludes the owner being created).\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired the step in after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 ignored the new target in `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (the field auto-maps into the DTO on the response side).\n\nThe persisted snapshot means the value returned at create time reads back identically on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 which is exactly what the acceptance test asserts (`$.bulkSignupWarning == false` for a fresh create under the threshold).",
